# Why this file exists, given package.json already has a `files` allowlist.
#
# When npm installs from a git URL it packs the checkout itself, and in that
# path it honours .gitignore. `/bin/fx-tests` is ignored there (it is generated),
# and npm was dropping the whole bin/ directory with it — so the installed
# package had no binary and the command it linked did not exist, while the same
# package installed from a tarball worked. The presence of a .npmignore makes
# npm use this file instead of .gitignore, which breaks that coupling.
#
# Keep it in step with `files` in package.json: this excludes, that includes,
# and the intersection is what ships. `npm pack --dry-run` prints the result.

# Sources: the published package runs the bundle in bin/, not the TypeScript.
cli/
lib/
tools/
test/

# The dashboards, which have nothing to do with the CLI.
*.html
*.css
*.svg
common-*.js
shared.js
fetch-utils.js
dashboards.js
profile-worker.js
fetch-xpcshell-data.js
mochitest-stats-backfill.json

# Development-only configuration.
tsconfig.json
.node-version
.github/
artifacts/

# The generated development entry point. bin/fx-tests.js and its map are the
# artefact that ships, and must not be excluded here.
bin/fx-tests
